author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: "The default npm metadata wait in verify-published-release.mjs is at least fifteen minutes, above the six-to-eight-minute lag measured on 2026-09-11 and 2026-09-12, and the usage text states the default; The release.yml verify step and job timeouts accommodate the longer wait and the ci-workflow contract spec pins the new job budget with the auto-release budget still at least thirty minutes larger; A unit spec proves the default attempt count without passing --npm-attempts; The next scheduled cut after the change passes attempt 1 or fails for a cause other than npm metadata propagation, recorded on pm-e70zh5"
parent: pm-u9d0
risk: low
confidence: high
severity: high
resolution: verify-published-release.mjs defaults to 60 npm metadata polls at 15 seconds (about fifteen minutes) instead of 20; release.yml verify step timeout 20 minutes and job timeout 60 minutes; ci-workflow-contract spec pins 60; a unit spec proves the default without passing --npm-attempts
expected_result: A scheduled cut whose publish-to-visible lag stays under fifteen minutes passes the Release workflow on attempt 1 with no manual re-run
actual_result: "Two consecutive scheduled cuts (2026-09-11, 2026-09-12) failed attempt 1 at E404 after five minutes while npm made the version visible after 8m14s and 6m10s; both were re-run by hand"
